 workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "development", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process of working on something to make it successful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: According to Bruce Tuckman, there are five phases of group development.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about groups. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sequential", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening in a set order", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Groups can go back and forth between the phases, so they should not be seen as sequential.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to arise", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin be caused or started by a situation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Questions arise among the group.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "preconceived", "type": "name"}, {"content": "formed before you have enough knowledge or experience", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the norming stage, members are willing to change their preconceived opinions in response to the ideas and facts introduced by the other members of the team. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "clique", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small group of people who do not want other people to join them  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cliques disappear and leadership is shared. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to solicit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask someone for help or information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It has been agreed to solicit and share feelings, accept constructive feedback, and explore the range of possible actions related to the task.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "emphasis", "type": "name"}, {"content": "special attention or importance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is decided to place emphasis on achievement through problem-solving, hard work and productivity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disengagement", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the process of withdrawing from involvement in a particular group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The final stage, adjourning, was suggested by Tuckman to include the disengagement from the task.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Passive -ing Forms ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use passive -ing forms (<span class=\"strong\">being</span> + <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">having been </span>+ <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span>) as participles.  These structures would imply the \"since\", \"because of\", \"due to\", \"owing to\" respectively.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Being paid</span> monthly, I find it hard to pay all my bills on time.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Having been moved</span> around as a child, she has no desire to do the same as an adult.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Being accepted in the group is key at this stage, so group members will observe each other carefully. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Having been accepted by the group, members start to warm up to one another. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Being given the opportunity, members say their personal goodbyes to each other. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to report a fact or belief, you can use a variety of ways to construct your ideas. When you do not want to mention the source of the information, you can use a passive structure.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the structure <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">It + passive verb + to-infinitive</span></span>. You can only use this pattern with the verbs <span class=\"italic\">agree</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> decide</span>, <span class=\"italic\">suggest</span> and <span class=\"italic\">propose</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It was agreed to promote</span> the whole team at once.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If necessary, you can express the agent.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">It was agreed <span class=\"strong\">by the managers</span> to promote the whole team at once.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " At this point, it has been agreed to solicit and share feelings, accept constructive feedback, and explore the range of possible actions related to the task.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " The final stage, adjourning, was suggested by Tuckman to include the disengagement from the task and the conclusion of relationships.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch a video on \u201cTuckman Stages of Group Development\u201d by Katy Jones online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get into groups of three or four.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a similar video explaining Tuckman's five stages of development on a phone or other video recording device. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Next, write about your experience working in the group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How did your group experience relate to the different stages of group development?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write your experience in a 200-word document.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I collaborate with a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I plan and make a video with group members.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I reflect on my experience working in the group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about my experience.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}